+### Proposed: one skill owns guard building
+
+**Status**: Proposed 2026-10-07 by an entropy-assessment run. Awaiting the steward; not in effect.
+**Context**: Two exportable skills build guards, with different output shapes. `skills/docs-first-planning-assessment/` Phase 2 designs a docs-first delta guard. `skills/session-coherence-skill-generator/` writes `skills/session-coherence-guard/SKILL.md` from its own template, and gained bootstrap mode in the entry "Session-coherence generation should bootstrap young repos…" below. `INTENT.md` "The guard lifecycle" names only `entropy-assessment` and `docs-first-planning-assessment` as the generator, the front door never routes to `session-coherence-skill-generator`, and `skills/guards-integrator/` still says it runs after `entropy-assessment` generates guards. No entry here decides which skill owns guard building.
+**Proposal**: Make `session-coherence-skill-generator` the only skill that writes guards. `docs-first-planning-assessment` Phase 2 supplies its docs-first checks to it, and `entropy-assessment` hands its profile and ranked risks to it. Alternatives considered: docs-first Phase 2 builds guards for docs-first repos and the generator only bootstraps young repos; or both stay as peers.
+**Impact if accepted**: Every repo in the validation batch gets one guard shape, so results compare. `INTENT.md` "The guard lifecycle", `README.md` "How to use this repo", the front door's next moves, docs-first Phase 2 and `guards-integrator` "When to Run" change to match.
+
