+### Proposed: what the validation batch measures
+
+**Status**: Proposed 2026-10-07 by an entropy-assessment run. Awaiting the steward; not in effect.
+**Context**: "Farm broader entropic-immunity exploration…" below says to track whether the validation loop "produces more merged PRs". `INTENT.md` "Scope boundary and next validation loop" (revised 2026-04-07) says to track "clearer session recovery, fewer reintroduced stale ideas, more coherent docs, and sharper feedback", and `README.md` "Project status" says "more useful changes in the wild". `TODO.md` Next Up says "track what changes prove useful". Nothing says whether merged PRs were dropped.
+**Proposal**: Track both for each batch repo: merged PRs from guard-driven changes as the outcome, and the session-quality observations from `INTENT.md` as the diagnosis.
+**Impact if accepted**: The validation record for each batch repo has both columns, and the four places that state the measure are reduced to `INTENT.md` plus links.
